refs={2:('bank-cla','101','B1'),3:('bank-cla','112','B2'),4:('bank-cla','114','B3'),5:('bank-cla','116','B4'),6:('bank-cla','121','B5'),7:('bank-cla','123','B7'),8:('nbfc-digital','6(7)','D1'),9:('nbfc-digital','10(3)','D2'),10:('nbfc-digital','25(4)','D8')}
for index,(sid,section,claim) in refs.items():
    for bank,prefix in [(cards,''),(questions,'q-')]:
        item=next(x for x in bank if x['id']==f'{prefix}controls-{index:02}')
        item['sources']=[dict(id=sid,section=section,claim=claim)]
        item['scope']='In-scope current commercial-bank Part B CLA' if sid=='bank-cla' else 'In-scope NBFC digital lending'
        item['checked']='2026-10-04'
        if index==10 and bank is cards: item['sources'].append(dict(id='nbfc-digital',section='25(2)',claim='D7'))
def case(cid,title,mid,scenario,steps,rows,checks):
    case_questions=[]
    pages=next(m['pages'] for m in modules if m['id']==mid)
    for i,line in enumerate(rows.strip().splitlines(),1):
        a=line.split('|'); assert len(a)==7,(cid,i,len(a))
        prompt,correct,why,w1,e1,w2,e2=a
        opts=[dict(text=correct,explanation=why),dict(text=w1,explanation=e1),dict(text=w2,explanation=e2)]
        shift=(len(questions)*7+1)%3; opts=opts[shift:]+opts[:shift]
        qid=f'q-{cid}-{i}'
        questions.append(dict(id=qid,module=mid,case=cid,prompt=prompt,options=opts,answer=(3-shift)%3,difficulty='Advanced',sources=[dict(id='guide',pages=pages),dict(id='original-case')],prerequisites=[m['id'] for m in modules[:modules.index(next(x for x in modules if x['id']==mid))]]))
        case_questions.append(qid)
    cases.append(dict(id=cid,title=title,module=mid,scenario=scenario,steps=steps,questions=case_questions,checks=checks,sources=[dict(id='guide',pages=pages),dict(id='original-case')]))
case('case-01','A bounced installment is not a principal repayment','schedules',
'Illustrative monthly ledger: loan ₹1,00,000, monthly reducing rate 1%, fixed payment ₹6,000. Round each month interest to paise. Month 1 is paid. Month 2 is billed but the collection fails. Ignore penalty fees and any extra interest on arrears for this exercise. Inclusive POS decreases only for actual principal repayments.',[
'Month 1 interest = 1,00,000 × 1% = ₹1,000; paid principal = 6,000 − 1,000 = ₹5,000. Actual and scheduled closing POS = ₹95,000.',
'Month 2 scheduled interest = 95,000 × 1% = ₹950; scheduled principal = ₹5,050. Scheduled closing would be ₹89,950 if paid.',
'No month 2 principal cash is collected. Actual inclusive POS remains ₹95,000. ₹5,050 is an overdue principal slice inside that POS, not a second asset to add.',
'Month 2 due total remains ₹6,000, separate from the not-yet-due principal. Do not use the schedule projection as proof of cash collection.'
],'''
In case 01, actual POS immediately after month 2 failure is what?|₹95,000|Only month 1 paid principal ₹5,000 reduced actual POS.|₹89,950|This is month 2 scheduled closing assuming successful payment.|₹1,00,000|This ignores the successful month 1 principal repayment.
In case 01, month 2 scheduled principal component is what?|₹5,050|₹6,000 payment less ₹950 interest gives ₹5,050.|₹6,000|This ignores interest.|₹950|This is interest, not principal.
In case 01, how much is actual POS above month 2 scheduled closing?|₹5,050|₹95,000 actual − ₹89,950 scheduled = ₹5,050 unpaid scheduled principal.|₹6,000|The due includes ₹950 interest that is not principal.|₹0|The collection failed, so actual and scheduled exposure diverge.
''',[dict(op='subtract',args=[100000,5000],expected=95000),dict(op='subtract',args=[6000,950],expected=5050),dict(op='subtract',args=[95000,5050],expected=89950)])
case('case-02','Two waterfalls, one conserved receipt','waterfalls',
'Two overdue buckets, A older than B. A: charge ₹100, interest ₹900, principal ₹3,000. B: charge ₹100, interest ₹800, principal ₹3,000. Payment ₹4,000. Vertical = oldest bucket, then charge→interest→principal. Horizontal = all charges oldest-first, then all interest oldest-first, then principal oldest-first. DPD tracks unpaid principal/interest.',[
'Total due = (100 + 900 + 3,000) + (100 + 800 + 3,000) = ₹7,900. Remaining aggregate after ₹4,000 = ₹3,900 in either policy.',
'Vertical: A consumes 100 + 900 + 3,000 = ₹4,000; A closes and B remains ₹3,900.',
'Horizontal: charges ₹200; interest ₹1,700; available for principal ₹2,100. A principal left ₹900; B principal left ₹3,000.',
'Under horizontal, A remains the oldest relevant unpaid bucket. Aggregate remaining debt is identical, but the oldest unpaid due is different.'
],'''
In case 02 horizontal allocation, A principal left is what?|₹900|₹4,000 − ₹200 charges − ₹1,700 interest = ₹2,100 principal payment; ₹3,000 − ₹2,100 = ₹900.|₹0|That is vertical A closure.|₹3,000|Horizontal does allocate some cash to A principal.
In case 02, aggregate remaining due under either policy is what?|₹3,900|₹7,900 total − ₹4,000 receipt = ₹3,900.|₹7,900|That ignores the payment.|₹4,000|That is payment, not residual dues.
In case 02, which policy fully clears the oldest relevant bucket A?|Vertical|A receives its full ₹4,000 under bucket-first order.|Horizontal|A still has ₹900 principal under component-first order.|Neither because payment is partial at loan level|A bucket can close even if the whole loan's dues remain partly unpaid.
''',[dict(op='sum',args=[100,900,3000,100,800,3000],expected=7900),dict(op='subtract',args=[7900,4000],expected=3900),dict(op='subtract',args=[3000,2100],expected=900)])
